e", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/SnuggleHug/", "num_games_owned": 281, "num_reviews": 26, "playtime_forever": 13320, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5008, "last_played": 1631506588, "avatar": "ee77874a316aaf9e89cd28bdac1c14b9d2a30378"}, "language": "english", "review": "Arma 3 is good but lacks a lot of content only 1 jet and lots of copy and pasting for all the game's armies. \n\nI feel like graphics were being worked on more than gameplay and content. AI is still stupid, no rpg backblast, no bipods/weapon resting, and just feels less realistic than Arma 2. I love the new animations, voice acting, and glorious !!RAGDOLLS!!. But still doesn't make up for the lack of content and no campaign yet. Of course the best thing about the arma series and arma 3 is the user created content, you can download and create your own missions and campaigns, weapons, vehicles, etc. And there are lots of mods that will improve basically every aspect of the game, such as ACE which will add more realism.\n\n So I would wait to buy it if you haven't already (I got my copy during alpha for around only $35) for the price to go down and for Bohema to release free DLC the have promised which will include the campaign and lots of other content. The game is off on a rough release but as with Arma 2, it will eventually develop into a beautiful game with endless content and entertainment value.", "timestamp_created": 1379798081, "timestamp_updated": 1379798081, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "2574742", "author": {"steamid": "76561198009466516", "personaname": "Chintilion", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198009466516/", "num_games_